    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n35931" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">phărē^trātus</span></b> ,
			a, um, adj.
		pharetra, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>furnished with</i> or <i>wearing a
				quiver</i>, <i>quivered</i> (<b>poet.</b>): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pharetrata Camilla,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					A. 11, 649</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Persis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. G.
					4, 290</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Geloni,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 3, 4, 35</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">puer,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Cupid</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov.
					M. 10, 525</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">virgo,</span>”
				i.e. <i>Diana</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Am. 1, 1, 10</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Semiramis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					2, 108</span></i>
			.</div>
